1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:05,050
When you crack your knuckles, that loud pop is NOT bones grinding together!

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:09,725
Inside your finger joints is a slippery liquid called synovial fluid.

3
00:00:09,725 --> 00:00:15,162
When you stretch your finger, pressure drops rapidly, creating an intense vacuum.

4
00:00:15,162 --> 00:00:20,687
In just three hundred milliseconds, a microscopic nitrogen gas bubble is born!

5
00:00:20,687 --> 00:00:26,512
The birth and collapse of that bubble unleashes a tiny shockwave: the loud crack you hear.

6
00:00:26,512 --> 00:00:31,550
It takes twenty full minutes for the gas to dissolve back before you can pop it again.

7
00:00:31,550 --> 00:00:36,137
And don't worry: science has proven it does not cause arthritis!

8
00:00:36,137 --> 00:00:38,825
How often do you crack your knuckles?

